## Overview
The Gold Layer serves as the final presentation layer, optimized for analytical workloads and business reporting. It contains dimension tables for descriptive attributes and fact tables for measurable business data.
---

1. gold_customers
Purpose: Contains customer information enhanced with demographic and geographic attributes for customer dimensions.


| Column Name      | Data Type     | Description                                                                                   |
|------------------|---------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| customer_key     | INT           | Internal surrogate key generated to uniquely represent a customer within the data warehouse.  |
| customer_id      | INT           | Original customer identifier sourced from the operational system.                             |
| customer_number  | NVARCHAR(50)  | Business-facing customer reference code used for identification and record management.        |
| firstname        | NVARCHAR(50)  | Customer's given name.                                                                        |
| lastname         | NVARCHAR(50)  | Customer's family or last name.                                                               |
| marital_status   | NVARCHAR(50)  | Current marital status associated with the customer.                                          |
| gender           | NVARCHAR(50)  | Gender information recorded for the customer.                                                 |
| country          | NVARCHAR(50)  | Nation in which the customer is located or resides.                                           |
| birthdate        | DATE          | Recorded date of birth of the customer.                                                       |
| create_date      | DATE          | Date when the customer profile was first added to the source system.                          |



2. gold_products_dimensions
Purpose: Holds product-related data along with key characteristics and attributes for product dimensions.


| Column Name         | Data Type     | Description                                                                                              |
|---------------------|---------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| product_key_num     | INT           | System-generated surrogate key used to uniquely identify each product record within the dimension table. |
| product_id          | INT           | Source-system identifier assigned to a product for unique identification.                                |
| product_key         | NVARCHAR(50)  | Business product code used for product identification, tracking, and inventory management.               |
| product_name        | NVARCHAR(50)  | Product title containing descriptive details such as model, color, or size.                              |
| category_id         | NVARCHAR(50)  | Unique code representing the product category.                                                           |
| category            | NVARCHAR(50)  | Primary classification used to group products into broad business categories.                            |
| subcategory         | NVARCHAR(50)  | Secondary classification that provides a more detailed grouping within a category.                       |
| maintenance         | NVARCHAR(50)  | Indicates whether the product requires ongoing maintenance or servicing.                                 |
| product_cost        | INT           | Cost value associated with the product before any sales markup or pricing adjustments.                   |
| product_line        | NVARCHAR(50)  | Product family or collection that identifies the series to which the product belongs.                    |
| product_start_date  | DATE          | Date when the product was introduced, launched, or made available for sale.                              |

---

3.gold_product_sales
Purpose: Captures sales transactions and measurable data to support business analysis and reporting as sales facts.

| Column Name        | Data Type     | Description                                                                                   |
|--------------------|---------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| sales_order_number | NVARCHAR(50)  | Unique alphanumeric reference assigned to each sales transaction.                             |
| product_key_num    | INT           | Surrogate key used to associate the sales record with the product dimension.                  |
| customer_key       | INT           | Surrogate key linking the transaction to the corresponding customer dimension.                |
| sales_order_date   | DATE          | Date on which the order was originally placed.                                                |
| sales_ship_date    | DATE          | Date on which the order was dispatched to the customer.                                       |
| sales_due_date     | DATE          | Scheduled payment due date for the order.                                                     |
| sales_sales        | INT           | Total revenue generated from the sales line item, recorded in currency units.                 |
| sales_quantity     | INT           | Number of product units included in the transaction.                                          |
| sales_price        | INT           | Unit price applied to the product for the sales line item.                                    |
